From: Eloi Rotava <eloi@rotava.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rt2x00: rt2800: MT7620 64 KB A-MPDU and vendor retry limits

The MediaTek driver for the MT7620 (RT6352) allows 64 KB A-MPDUs
(MAX_PSDU 3) and uses 15/31 hardware retries.  rt2x00 used 16 KB and
the mac80211 limits.

NOT MEASURABLY BETTER: repeated A/B runs on 2026-10-14 (Archer C5 v4,
A71 at -63 dBm, channels 11 and 13) gave the stock settings the same
22-26 Mbit/s.  Kept off.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2800lib.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ralink/rt2x00/rt2800lib.c
@@ -6047,6 +6047,9 @@
 	rt2x00_set_field32(&reg, MAX_LEN_CFG_MAX_MPDU, AGGREGATION_SIZE);
 	if (rt2x00_is_usb(rt2x00dev)) {
 		drv_data->max_psdu = 3;
+	} else if (rt2x00_rt(rt2x00dev, RT6352)) {
+		/* 64 KB, like the MediaTek driver for the MT7620 */
+		drv_data->max_psdu = 3;
 	} else if (rt2x00_rt_rev_gte(rt2x00dev, RT2872, REV_RT2872E) ||
 		   rt2x00_rt(rt2x00dev, RT2883) ||
 		   rt2x00_rt_rev_lt(rt2x00dev, RT3070, REV_RT3070E)) {
@@ -11714,6 +11717,16 @@
 	rt2x00dev->hw->wiphy->retry_long = 2;
 
 	/*
+	 * The MT7620 vendor driver retries much more in hardware (15/31);
+	 * with the low limits the many retries of this radio turn into
+	 * lost frames and TCP throughput collapses.
+	 */
+	if (rt2x00_rt(rt2x00dev, RT6352)) {
+		rt2x00dev->hw->wiphy->retry_short = 15;
+		rt2x00dev->hw->wiphy->retry_long = 31;
+	}
+
+	/*
 	 * Initialize all hw fields.
 	 */
 	ieee80211_hw_set(rt2x00dev->hw, REPORTS_TX_ACK_STATUS);
